they cannot be treated on the island.

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:51.020
They still have to leave.

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:53.940
And just getting this non-tertiary building constructed

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:56.060
was a bureaucratic nightmare.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:59.300
The sources reference a RAND reconstruction report

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:01.420
detailing how Puerto Rico's recovery is plagued

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.980
by a split bureaucracy.

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:06.740
Yes, the coordination was practically non-existent.

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:08.660
For this specific hospital,

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:10.340
the infrastructure financing authority

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:12.540
handled the actual construction.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:15.580
General services was supposed to buy the medical equipment

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:16.820
and the Department of Health

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:19.020
was in charge of operations and licensing.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:21.180
You have hundreds of sub-recipients

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:23.220
and almost no single accountable person

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:26.740
empowered to force a deadline across all those agencies.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:29.140
Here's where it gets really interesting.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:31.340
Building this hospital was like trying to drive a car

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:33.180
with four different steering wheels,

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:34.940
all controlled by different departments

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:36.780
who refused to talk to each other.

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:38.540
That's exactly what it was like.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:39.380
The result?

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:42.060
Local reporting noted the physical building was finished

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:43.980
and handed over to the health department

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:46.340
months before it even had a medical staff

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:47.980
or a firm opening date.

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:49.260
Which is just wild.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:51.820
Which brings me back to my opening thought.

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:53.620
If they were celebrating this beautiful

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:55.820
FAA certified heliport,

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:57.820
isn't that just an architectural admission

00:13:57.820 --> 00:14:01.340
that they still can't treat serious trauma locally?

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:02.740
It's literally a launchpad

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:05.140
to get you away from the hospital they just built.

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:07.780
As the investigative briefing Isla Naina phrased it,

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:09.620
the heliport is an admission of failure

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:10.900
dressed as a ribbon.

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:11.740
Wow.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:12.900
A building is just a monument

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:14.580
if it doesn't have doctors inside it.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:16.300
And to understand why recruiting

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:18.540
and keeping those doctors is so difficult,

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:21.100
we have to pivot away from local construction politics

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:23.820
and look at the invisible engine I mentioned earlier.

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:25.580
National payment formulas.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:26.940
Right, because you can build the nicest

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:28.380
heliport in the world.

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.020
But if the hospital system can't afford

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:31.460
to pay a trauma surgeon,

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:33.100
that helipad is just concrete.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.100
Exactly.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:35.900
And this is where Secretary Kennedy

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:39.260
is really in the hot seat regarding Medicare Advantage.

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:40.660
I need you to break this down for us

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:42.740
because this is where the policy

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:45.900
actually dictates who lives and who dies.

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:48.220
The crux of the financial crisis for Puerto Rico

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:51.300
is its Medicare Advantage or MA enrollment.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:53.580
Puerto Rico has the highest MA enrollment

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:54.860
in the entire country.

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:55.700
Really?

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:56.540
The highest?

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:57.780
By far.

00:14:57.780 --> 00:15:01.180
We are talking about roughly 670,000 beneficiaries

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:05.060
which is about 96% of all Medicare enrollees on the island.

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:06.660
96%.

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:09.020
So the entire island's medical economy

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:11.620
relies on this one federal formula?

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:14.500
How exactly does the formula starve them?

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:16.500
It comes down to how the federal government

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.460
calculates the baseline payment

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:22.020
known as the Average Geographic Amount or AGA.

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:23.340
Okay, AGA.

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:26.740
Historically, this formula is tied to traditional fee-for-service

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:28.780
Medicare spending in a given region.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:30.700
But Puerto Rico has historically had

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.860
very low traditional Medicare spending,

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:35.540
partly due to different demographic profiles

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:38.020
and a historical lack of automatic enrollment

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:39.340
in Medicare Part B.

00:15:39.340 --> 00:15:42.460
So because the baseline history is low,

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:44.780
the formula punishes them moving forward?

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:47.460
Exactly, it creates an artificial ceiling.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.740
It's a self-fulfilling prophecy.

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.780
Because they were underfunded in the past,

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:53.660
the formula dictates they must remain

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:55.580
underfunded in the future.

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:57.100
Exactly the issue.

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:59.580
The result is that Puerto Rico's Medicare Advantage rates

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:02.340
are roughly 41% below the national average.

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:03.860
41%.

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:05.980
They're even 20% below the neighboring

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:07.860
United States Virgin Islands.

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:10.100
And despite this massive glaring gap,

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:13.300
the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services, CMS,

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:17.460
only granted a 4.01% increase for 2027.

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:22.340
Wait, they gave them 4% to try and close a 41% gap?

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:23.300
Basically, yes.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:25.380
Which is mathematically nowhere near enough.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:26.500
It's like being told,

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.500
you have to run a Michelin star hospital,

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:30.300
but you're only given the grocery budget

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.620
for a fast food drive-through.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:32.980
It's impossible.

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:35.220
And the political pressure on this specific formula

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.780
is boiling over.

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:40.140
According to the sources, on August 3rd, 2026,

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:43.100
Representative Greg Murphy led a group of 13 Republicans

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:46.220
sending a letter directly to HHS Secretary Kennedy.

00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:47.580
Right, a very pointed letter.

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:51.100
They were demanding that Kennedy address this rigged formula.

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:53.060
Specifically, they wanted to level up

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:56.820
that average geographic amount to a 0.70 floor,

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:58.420
meaning at the very least,

00:16:58.420 --> 00:17:01.540
Puerto Rico should get 70% of the national average.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:03.420
And Governor González-Colón

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:05.780
has also publicly pressed Kennedy on these benchmarks.

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:07.500
It's coming from all sides.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.580
If we connect this to the bigger picture,

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:11.780
if that wasn't enough financial pressure

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:14.700
looming directly behind this Medicare Advantage fight

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.420
is a massive Medicaid cliff

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:19.860
that Puerto Rico is gonna face on September 30th, 2027.

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:21.220
Let's define that for the listener

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:24.620
because a Medicaid cliff sounds catastrophic.

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:28.020
What actually happens on September 30th, 2027?

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:29.260
A Medicaid cliff happens

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:32.900
when temporary supplemental federal funding boosts expire.

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:35.460
Puerto Rico's Medicaid system relies heavily

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:37.780
on these temporary federal injections.

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:41.620
On September 30th, 2027, unless Congress acts,

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:43.580
that temporary funding vanishes

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.540
and Puerto Rico reverts to a strict,

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:48.180
structurally inadequate statutory cap.

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:49.020
Wow.

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:51.100
It's the equivalent of your household salary

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:53.340
suddenly being cut by 80% overnight

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:56.860
while your mortgage and utility bills stay the exact same.

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:59.740
It threatens to collapse the entire safety net.

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:02.420
If we look at this from a distance, you know,

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:04.900
you begin to see why the local investigative journalists

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:07.700
are so deeply cynical about a ribbon cutting ceremony.

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:08.700
Oh, without a doubt.

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:10.220
A beautiful new emergency room

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:13.860
on an underpaid island is nothing more than a stage set.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:16.180
You cannot recruit a night shift physician

00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:18.660
or a specialized technician to move to an island

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:19.860
with expensive groceries

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:22.780
and notoriously unreliable ferry transport

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.580
if the federal reimbursement formula

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:26.660
structurally starves the payroll.

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:29.020
The math fundamentally does not work.

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:32.420
So we've diagnosed the architectural contradiction,

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:36.020
a hospital that isn't really equipped as a full hospital

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:37.940
and the financial catch 22,

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:40.340
a system designed to underpay the very doctors

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:42.100
it desperately needs.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:43.980
What is the actual prescription here?

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:45.420
Right, how do we fix it?

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:46.940
Yeah, how do we ensure this building

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:50.900
isn't just a 2026 photo op that slowly decays?

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:51.940
The critical briefings

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:54.940
outline a very stringent set of demands, receipts,

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:57.100
they call them, for all the stakeholders involved.

00:18:57.100 --> 00:18:57.940
Let's break them down

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.220
because they finish strong with these recommendations

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:01.940
starting with the federal government.

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:03.700
What do they want from Washington?

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:06.300
The primary demand to the federal government is direct.

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:08.380
Do not visit the island every 20 years

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:10.900
after you left just to cut a ribbon and leave.

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:12.340
They are demanding the publication

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:16.060
of a weekly public operating dashboard within 30 days.

00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:18.420
A dashboard tracking what exactly?

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:21.060
Are we talking about patient outcomes or staffing?

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:23.660
Tracking the actual operational reality.

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:26.540
How many night shift doctors are physically on the island?

00:19:26.540 --> 00:19:29.660
What is the dialysis uptime versus canceled hours?

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:32.340
Are the CT scanners actually licensed and staffed

00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:34.060
or just sitting in a box?

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:35.340
Transparency.

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:37.300
Okay, what about the local government?

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:38.780
For the local government in San Juan,

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:41.780
the demand is do not make Vieques a photo opportunity

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:44.580
and do not leave the hospital without proper funding.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.500
Which is easier said than done.

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.060
They demand that the operating money

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:50.780
be separated into a locked five year appropriations

00:19:50.780 --> 00:19:52.860
so the central government can't raid the funds

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:54.020
for other agencies.

00:19:54.020 --> 00:19:54.980
Smart.

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:57.460
I read the demands for the healthcare providers too.

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:59.060
The mandate for the doctors and nurses

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:01.060
is to do your best to stay on Vieques

00:20:01.060 --> 00:20:03.060
and give the best service possible

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:05.060
but they are explicitly told to refuse

00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:06.900
to accept ghost rosters.

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:08.780
Right, the ghost rosters.

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:11.340
For those outside the medical administration field,

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:13.380
a ghost roster is when a hospital lists

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:15.780
a bunch of specialists on their official paperwork

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:17.500
to pass a credentialing inspection

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:19.740
but those doctors aren't actually in the building

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:21.460
or taking local appointments.

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:22.940
It's a huge problem.

00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:24.940
The community is demanding that all credentialing

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:26.980
is completely legitimate and finished

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:29.340
before the very first ambulance arrives.

00:20:29.340 --> 00:20:31.900
Furthermore, medically they need to practice the medicine

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:33.700
the island actually requires,

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:36.580
meaning treat the dialysis, the diabetes,

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:38.900
the hypertension and the mental health trauma

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:41.100
from decades of environmental stress.

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:42.940
Don't just make it look good for a brochure.

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:43.940
Exactly.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:46.380
Do not import flashy mainland service lines

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:48.460
just to make a hospital brochure look good

00:20:48.460 --> 00:20:50.100
while ignoring the chronic conditions

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:51.940
that are actually filling the waiting room.

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:53.580
And finally there are instructions

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.540
for the patients in the general public.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:56.980
Yes, very important ones.

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:59.380
The sources advise the patients in general public

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:03.620
to be patient, to form a public patients council

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:06.780
and to stay tuned to the healthcare paradox.

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:09.500
They want every single missed specialist appointment

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:11.780
or emergency room diversion logged.

00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:13.300
Keep the receipts.

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:16.060
And here is a really profound point from the briefings.

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:19.500
Treat geography as clinical infrastructure.

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:21.900
If a dialysis patient misses a lifesaving session

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:25.020
because a ferry didn't sail, that is a clinical incident.

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:27.140
It is not a transportation excuse.

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:29.700
That reframing is so powerful.

00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:32.940
But I have to ask you, looking at the history

00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:36.300
we just covered, wait, sorry.

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:39.580
Looking at the history we just covered,

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:42.420
are these recommendations actually realistic?

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:44.260
Or are they just a desperate attempt

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:47.380
to force a fundamentally broken bureaucratic machine

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:49.900
to act like it actually cares?

00:21:49.900 --> 00:21:51.900
It is an attempt to enforce accountability

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:53.220
through visibility.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:54.860
Secretary Kennedy himself learned

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:57.220
in that Guainabo jail cell 25 years ago

00:21:57.220 --> 00:22:00.460
that outside attention is strictly temporary.

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:02.740
Celebrities, politicians, cabinet secretaries,

00:22:02.740 --> 00:22:03.660
they always fly home.

00:22:03.660 --> 00:22:04.980
The cameras always leave.

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:06.660
But the night shift remains.

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:08.660
Local persistence was the only force

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:10.460
that kept the Navy debate alive back then

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:11.540
and it is the only force

00:22:11.540 --> 00:22:13.820
that will keep this new hospital honest today.

00:22:13.820 --> 00:22:15.620
So what does this whole mean?

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:17.420
We started by looking at a ribbon cutting

00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:20.580
for an $85.5 million hospital.

00:22:20.580 --> 00:22:23.020
But as we've seen, this deep dive

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:25.300
isn't just about one island in the Caribbean.

00:22:25.300 --> 00:22:26.500
No, it's so much bigger.

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:29.580
It's a masterclass in how federal payment formulas,

00:22:29.580 --> 00:22:32.260
political photo ops and local persistence

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:35.460
violently collide to shape human survival.

00:22:35.460 --> 00:22:37.060
It is undeniably wonderful

00:22:37.060 --> 00:22:39.260
that a child in VA case may no longer die

00:22:39.260 --> 00:22:41.380
simply for lack of a ventilator.

00:22:41.380 --> 00:22:43.820
But it is deeply cynical that it took a death,

00:22:43.820 --> 00:22:45.820
a lawsuit, nine years,

00:22:45.820 --> 00:22:47.740
and a cabinet secretary's visit

00:22:47.740 --> 00:22:48.900
to deliver a standard of care

00:22:48.900 --> 00:22:51.900
that other American towns consider perfectly ordinary.

00:22:51.900 --> 00:22:54.300
Gratitude and suspicion can and should

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:56.020
occupy the same sentence here.

00:22:56.060 --> 00:22:57.900
The true test isn't the ribbon.

00:22:57.900 --> 00:22:59.980
The true test is whether Secretary Kennedy

00:22:59.980 --> 00:23:02.540
will actually fix the Medicare Advantage formula,

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:06.140
level up that AGA to the requested 0.70 floor

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:09.220
and address the looming 2027 Medicaid cliff.

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:11.460
If those systemic financial flaws aren't fixed,

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:13.780
this was just expensive architecture.

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:16.740
Which leads us with a final thought for you to mull over.

00:23:16.740 --> 00:23:19.540
If systemic healthcare equity requires constant,

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:21.900
unyielding local persistence,

00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:24.580
tracking fairies, logging missed appointments,

00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:26.780
begging for fair national funding formulas

00:23:26.780 --> 00:23:28.860
just to prevent officials from cutting a ribbon

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:30.380
and walking away,

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:32.780
what does that mean for other marginalized communities

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:35.220
waiting for their own ribbon cuttings?

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:37.500
It's a sobering question.

00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:39.540
Is equitable healthcare even possible

00:23:39.540 --> 00:23:42.020
under our current bureaucratic architecture?

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:44.020
Or will it always require a tragedy

00:23:44.020 --> 00:23:46.620
to force the state to remember you?

00:23:46.620 --> 00:23:48.980
Think back to our absentee landlord.

00:23:48.980 --> 00:23:51.020
The tarp is finally on the roof,

00:23:51.020 --> 00:23:52.580
but it's going to take a lot more

00:23:52.580 --> 00:23:54.300
than a parade to prove the storm

00:23:54.300 --> 00:23:55.900
is actually over.

